\subsection*{Comment}

A solution must either exhibit a nondegradable channel whose complementary
private capacity vanishes after regularization, or prove
$\mathfrak D=\mathfrak L_\infty$.  Determining whether the Belzig et al.
flagged channel remains less noisy under every tensor power would resolve this
problem or separate $\mathfrak L_\infty$ from $\mathfrak L_1$.

